**Correction to the numbers above.** Round 2 of the checker (local branch `nowset`, tip `934edf9df`) stopped refusing a correct paging cursor read: `_pages <p>.next` under `_when <p>.partial`, which is how `agent/src/Tool/Pages.ts` pages. Over the same 778 stored plans the refusal set now flags **66/276 failing and 0/502 passing**, not 73/276.

It is **no longer a superset of ZERO's lint** (72/0): both flag 65, the checker alone 1, ZERO alone 7. Six of those seven wait on a gated second page with no `<|>` fallback, which the checker reports as `conditional:gate` rather than refusing; the seventh has no finding left. Round 1's superset held only because of the unsound cursor rule.

The attached `NOWSET_TREE_PROPOSAL.md` and its pointer to `0643caa60` are superseded by `934edf9df`. The proposal itself (the core in `tree/src/plan/readcheck.ts` beside `whoCanWake`) and the four questions are unchanged.

**Scope's ticket folds into this one.** [IDE-124](https://linear.app/idealic/issue/IDE-124) lands the prototype in agent's eval tree and then closes as evidence here, so the checker's future is decided in one place. Open items, for Carrier's call alongside the four questions:
- a per-read report printer: today only counts are printed, and the per-read line is a test helper;
- nothing typechecks `agent/eval/` today;
- does a `Tool.pages` tool's answer always carry `pageInfo`? This decides whether `pageInfo` reads are conditional or unsatisfiable;
- gate comparison is text-based and leaks false negatives: `and` split with no precedence, any `??` taken as cover, alternatives matched as substrings (`$state.p` inside `$state.p2`), and any complementary pair treated as making every gated writer certain. None of these can refuse a plan, but they hide waits.

Round 2 proof (opens on the operator's machine): http://127.0.0.1:9440/proofs/proofs/invizko/nowset-r2-9a806951.html

