### 🧾 Untaught, cheap models write JavaScript kit refuses; taught, they fail on a short list of language gaps
- **Reported by**: PLANLANG lane for Yaroslaff Fedin, from LANGX-A · **Date**: 2026-10-20 (measured 2026-10-19)
- **Refs**: kit promptlab-tools `1d16a6ce8` · gemini-flash-latest thinking off · gpt-6-luna effort none
- **Attachments**: the proof page is local-only (opens on the operator's machine): http://127.0.0.1:9440/proofs/proofs/invizko/langx-a-natural-forms-71c6e0f1.html — the same page is uploaded below as `builds/langx-a-natural-forms_PROOF.html`; the lane log is `builds/langx/A_LOG.md`

[📄 langx-a-natural-forms_PROOF.html](https://uploads.linear.app/963aea4d-374d-4346-8fa1-9d10e8a5af04/4cf5dcdb-7453-4b41-8261-8417b1bed7ef/352e7594-6c09-4b7e-8e38-bc6b387d89af)

**The gap**: taught plans fail on capabilities the language lacks or spells differently: a pipe over `.` in a nested position, windows, multi-key sort, null-safe parsing, matching against several patterns — plus silent traps where kit's answer differs from a JavaScript reading.

**Evidence** (2026-10-19):
- 0 of 152 untaught JavaScript-form texts (arrows, methods, globals) compile;
- taught nested-pipe tasks compile 0 of 8 each (A06, A07); the window task passes 0 of 16;
- silent traps measured by probe: `round(x, 2)` answers 0 for 1/3; `capture` with no match gives `{}`, so a joined result reads "null/null" — luna shipped that answer; `"12" == 12` is false; a null key silently drops a row from a real answer;
- every taught string-parsing plan (8 of 8) wrote 3–11 regex alternatives, 7 of 8 with an explicit fallback;
- Finch's git log: 876 of 2,971 commits with references (29.5%) carry two id formats — the case for ordered-fallback matching;
- spend $0.439 billed over 297 rows.

**Why it matters**: each gap points at a specific move — accept, rewrite, refuse with a named fix, teach, or add a helper (a `match` with ordered fallbacks is sketched as a proposal to Carrier, with its falsifier).
